WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:05.080
Narrator: Americans love beer.

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:07.880
On average, 42% of them prefer it

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:10.030
to any other kind of alcohol,

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:11.700
so you might not be shocked to hear

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.750
that according to multiple studies,

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:17.220
over half of American
adults have a beer gut.

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:21.340
But don't swear off your
Friday-night cold one just yet

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:25.053
because it's not beer
specifically that's to blame.

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:30.710
Apple or hourglass, oval
or inverted triangle,

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:33.640
everyone has their own body shape,

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:36.180
and that's partially
because people store fat

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.380
in different places

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:40.110
depending on their genetics and hormones.

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:42.990
For women, popular spots
include the thighs,

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:45.200
arms, and backside,

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:49.031
while men tend to store
fat in their bellies.

00:00:49.031 --> 00:00:52.000
Much of it is a type of
fat called visceral fat,

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.750
which lurks deep within the stomach.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:57.120
In men, visceral fat tends to pile up

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:01.010
behind the abdominal wall where
it pushes the abs outward,

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:03.980
creating a protruding beer belly.

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:05.630
Though that name, "beer belly,"

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:07.100
is kind of a misnomer

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:10.780
because beer bellies aren't
exclusive to beer drinkers.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:13.050
That's because the problem
isn't the actual beer.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:15.210
It's the calories inside it.

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:17.040
On average, your favorite ale

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.810
contains around 150 calories per can.

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:22.780
That's 30 to 50 more calories

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:25.070
than a 5-ounce glass of wine

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:28.350
and 45 more than a shot of whiskey.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:29.700
And if you don't burn them off,

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:32.890
those extra calories can
go straight to your gut.

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:35.070
But not only do the
number of calories matter,

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:37.330
but the kind of calories.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:41.240
Beer contains high levels
of processed carbs,

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:44.230
which research shows can
interfere with insulin levels

00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:47.290
and promote fat storage
around your organs.

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:49.830
And while a serving of wine, for instance,

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:53.280
contains just 1 or 2 grams of carbs,

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:56.820
a serving of beer contains 10 to 20.

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:59.500
It doesn't really matter
whether these calories and carbs

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:01.320
come from beer specifically

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:04.112
or from some other kind of junk food.

00:02:04.112 --> 00:02:05.053
So the good news is

00:02:05.053 --> 00:02:08.620
beer in moderation shouldn't
give you a beer belly.

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:11.220
That being said, no matter
where it comes from,

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:14.300
a beer belly is bad news.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.510
That's because visceral fat
wraps around your kidneys,

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:18.860
liver, and intestines

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:20.280
and releases hormones

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:23.040
that can disrupt their normal function,

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.120
and that can lead to issues
like Type 2 diabetes,

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.950
heart disease, and even cancer.

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:30.190
If that's not bad enough,

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:33.930
once your belly runs out of
room to store that visceral fat,

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:38.640
your body might start building
it up inside nearby organs,

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:42.470
which can lead to fatty liver
disease and other issues.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:45.670
In fact, one study found
that men with beer bellies

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:48.770
or a waste-to-hip ratio over 0.9

00:02:49.858 --> 00:02:53.430
had a 87% higher risk for death

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:55.710
than those who carried
the same amount of fat

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:57.900
in other parts of their body.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:00.475
87%, that's right.

00:03:00.475 --> 00:03:02.520
So even if you're otherwise skinny,

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:05.900
a spare tire can threaten your life.

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:08.470
And guys are more likely to grow a gut

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:10.910
as they get older because testosterone,

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:15.910
a sex hormone that helps keep
men slim, decreases with age.

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:19.460
While it's fun to joke about
your developing dad bod,

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:23.420
maybe just stick to having
one or two brewskis a night

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:25.920
instead of the whole six-pack.

